{"kind":"request","text":"The read-only clone preparation cc72e736 is complete and requester-adopted by 78a141ac. It identifies further HistorySource/CLI/receipt/trust decisions; none is silently settled by this request. Please first decide this small next dependency, after the current layout review:\n\nProposed first slice: an internal Node-only, read-only archive object transport and exact native journal-ref resolver, using the landed explicit-format object source contract. No HistorySource, portable package export, CLI option, text lookup, verifier/judge change, producer or provider call yet. It enables the later clone source without broadening legacy SHA-1 Reader/repositorySource/nodeExec behavior.\n\nThe transport receives an absolute repository directory, an explicit caller-owned JournalWork/original structural budget, and downward-only command options. It discovers storage format from bounded canonical Git metadata, accepting only sha1/sha256 and never inferring it from an ID length. Resolve only refs/artroom/journal/\u003cvalidated native scope ID\u003e; never enumerate unrelated refs, peel tags implicitly or fetch missing objects. Return the exact object ID, with actual commit/type/head validation still owed to the caller.\n\nCommands use argument arrays, the existing hardened configuration/environment and no shell, credentials, replacement objects, lazy network fetch, hooks, working-tree reads or clone-derived filesystem joins. Retain existing legacy process behavior; add a bounded Node execution path here. Bound combined captured stdout/stderr before holding chunks. Proposed metadata stdout ceiling 1 KiB, stderr 1 KiB, each body stdout bounded by the caller's exact requested limit and the existing 8 MiB object ceiling. A zero-limit object call probes metadata only and never starts a nonempty body read. Validate fixed metadata field counts, canonical ID/type/size and raw owned body bytes.\n\nEvery metadata/ref/format/body command spends the SAME supplied b